cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data, please cite it pinned to the commit you actually used. See README.md for the permalink format."
title: "Benchmark Nusantara"
type: dataset
version: "unreleased"
authors:
  - family-names: "Huda"
    given-names: "M. Khoirul"
    website: "https://mkhuda.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ibahasa/benchmark-nusantara"
url: "https://ibahasa.com/id/benchmark"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - Indonesian
  - Javanese
  - language model evaluation
  - low-resource languages
abstract: >
  Benchmark data for Indonesian and Javanese language models. Six sets covering
  slang comprehension, text normalisation, spelling correction, Javanese speech
  levels, and Javanese word meanings. Open items
  are graded by a native speaker under a published rubric. Four sets withhold
  roughly 30 per cent of their items from publication so that figures remain
  defensible against training-set contamination; the two sets that publish their
  full answer keys say so, carry a contamination canary, and are backed by a
  separate control set that is never published. See README.md for the limits of
  each set and CONTRIBUTING.md for how to dispute a figure.
